**1. POSITION VACANT: Program Director – Livelihoods, American India Foundation Trust (AIF), Delhi**

**2. ORGANISATIONAL BACKGROUND:**

**The American India Foundation Trust (AIF)**
is committed to advancing social and economic mobility for India’s most underserved communities, with a sustained focus on women, children, and youth. The Foundation does this through high-impact, scalable interventions across education, public health, and livelihoods, addressing multidimensional barriers to enable individuals to participate fully in India’s growth story. Founded two decades ago in the aftermath of the devastating Gujarat earthquake as a historic humanitarian initiative by then Prime Minister of India, Atal Bihari Vajpayee Ji, and U.S. President Mr. Bill Clinton, AIF has served 20.47 million lives across 35 States and Union Territories of India.

Registered as a Trust in India with an independent Board of Trustees, AIF adheres to rigorous financial and governance standards, ensuring transparency, accountability, and the responsible stewardship of resources. In strict compliance with Indian statutory and regulatory frameworks, AIF is registered under 12A, 80G, and the Foreign Contribution Regulation Act (FCRA), validating the organization’s institutional credibility and legal compliance. Learn more at www.aif-india.org

**About Livelihoods:**

**AIF’s**
Livelihoods Program expands economic opportunities for underserved communities by connecting youth, women, Persons with Disabilities (PwDs), artisans, and street vendors to market-relevant skills, entrepreneurship, financial inclusion, and dignified employment. Since 2006, the program has partnered with governments, industry, and local institutions to strengthen inclusive livelihood ecosystems that improve workforce participation, enterprise development, and long-term economic resilience.

Leveraging technology, industry partnerships, and market linkages, the program equips individuals with the technical, entrepreneurial, and digital skills needed to access opportunities across formal, informal, and emerging sectors. By promoting women’s economic participation, disability inclusion, and climate-resilient livelihoods, AIF enables underserved communities to build sustainable incomes and economic mobility. Since inception, the program has reached over 3.9 million people across India.

**3. JOB DESCRIPTION/ RESPONSIBILITIES:**

The
**Program Director**
, reporting to the
**Country Director**
, will provide strategic and operational leadership for the organisation’s portfolio of programmes in skilling, employability and entrepreneurship development. The incumbent will be accountable for the effective planning, implementation, quality, performance and impact of the programs under their portfolio.

The role will lead the program portfolio across the complete program lifecycle — from program planning and resource allocation through implementation, monitoring, evaluation, learning and scale-up. The incumbent will work closely with program teams, implementation partners, government and other relevant stakeholders to ensure that programs achieve their intended outcomes and deliver measurable impact.

The
**Program Director**
will provide leadership to program teams, strengthen program systems and processes, monitor program and budget performance, identify implementation risks and ensure timely corrective action. The incumbent will also contribute program expertise and inputs to donor and stakeholder engagements relating to the programs under their portfolio.

**Key Job Responsibilities:**

**A. Program Strategy & Leadership**

(1) Provide strategic direction and leadership for the portfolio of programs in skilling, employability and entrepreneurship development;

(2) Translate program strategy and organisational priorities into clear program objectives, outcomes, implementation plans and performance targets;

(3) Provide overall oversight to the planning, implementation and performance of programs/projects under the portfolio;

(4) Ensure that program design and implementation are responsive to beneficiary needs, sector priorities and project objectives;

(5) Lead periodic program reviews and provide strategic guidance to program teams to address challenges and improve program performance;

(6) Identify opportunities for program innovation, strengthening, replication and scale;

(7) Ensure that program-level operational, financial, compliance and implementation risks are identified and appropriately mitigated;

(8) Ensure effective coordination and integration across programs wherever relevant.

**B. Program Planning, Implementation & Quality**

(1) Lead the development and review of program implementation plans, milestones, deliverables and outcome targets;

(2) Ensure effective and timely implementation of programs in accordance with approved plans, budgets and agreed quality standards;

(3) Monitor program progress and ensure timely corrective action where implementation is off track;

(4) Strengthen program systems, processes and operating practices to improve quality, consistency and effectiveness;

(5) Ensure appropriate documentation of program processes, outputs, outcomes and learnings;

(6) Promote innovation and adoption of effective approaches and best practices across programs;

(7) Ensure that program implementation remains aligned with approved project objectives and commitments.

**C. Monitoring, Evaluation, Learning & MIS**

(1) Provide oversight to monitoring, evaluation and learning systems across the program portfolio;

(2) Ensure that program MIS, data and documentation are accurate, timely and effectively utilised for program decision-making;

(3) Review program performance against agreed outputs, outcomes, milestones and impact indicators;

(4) Use program data and evidence to identify trends, gaps, risks and opportunities for improvement;

(5) Promote a culture of continuous learning through periodic program reviews, knowledge-sharing forums and documentation of good practices;

(6) Ensure that program learnings and evidence inform program design and implementation;

(7) Ensure timely preparation and submission of project progress reports and other program-related reports as required;

(8) Ensure that feedback from evaluations, program reviews and stakeholders is translated into appropriate program improvements.

**D. Program Partnerships & Stakeholder Engagement**

(1) Build and maintain effective relationships with government departments, implementation partners, employers, academic and technical institutions and other stakeholders relevant to program delivery;

(2) Strengthen program partnerships that contribute to effective implementation, quality, reach and impact;

(3) Represent the program portfolio at relevant sector platforms, consultations, conferences and forums;

(4) Facilitate collaboration and knowledge exchange with relevant external stakeholders to strengthen program outcomes;

(5) Participate in donor and stakeholder discussions relating to programs under the portfolio and provide program-related inputs, updates and insights;

(6) Contribute program expertise to the development and refinement of project proposals and program concepts, as required.

**E. Program Resource & Budget Management**

(1) Ensure appropriate resource planning for programs in line with approved project plans, deliverables and budgets;

(2) Work closely with Finance to monitor program budgets, expenditure and utilisation against approved project allocations;

(3) Ensure effective and efficient utilisation of resources allocated to programs;

(4) Review program-level financial performance and identify significant variances, risks and corrective actions;

(5) Ensure that program teams adhere to applicable financial controls, donor requirements and approved budgets;

(6) Provide inputs into program budgets, costing and resource requirements during program design, planning and scale-up;

(7) Ensure that program implementation is aligned with approved financial and resource plans.

**F. Program Team Leadership & Development**

(1) Determine program staffing requirements based on program scope, implementation plans, deliverables and approved budgets;

(2) Build and lead high-performing, collaborative and results-oriented program teams;

(3) Provide strategic direction, coaching and mentoring to program leaders and team members;

(4) Establish clear goals, accountabilities and performance expectations for program teams;

95) Ensure timely performance reviews and effective performance management in line with organisational guidelines;

(6) Identify program team capability-building requirements and work with HR and relevant stakeholders to address them;

(7) Foster a culture of ownership, collaboration, learning, innovation and accountability within program teams;

(8) Strengthen the leadership capacity of program teams to support effective delivery and scale.

**G. Program Scale, Sustainability & Impact**

(1) Identify opportunities to strengthen, replicate and scale successful program models;

(2) Assess program performance, evidence and learnings to inform decisions on program expansion, redesign or consolidation;

(3) Identify opportunities to improve program efficiency, effectiveness, reach and beneficiary outcomes;

(4) Work with relevant program stakeholders to strengthen the sustainability and long-term impact of interventions;

(5) Promote evidence-based approaches to program development and scale;

(6) Ensure that program learning and evidence inform future program strategy, design and implementation.

**Key Accountabilities:**

(1) Achievement of agreed program/project outcomes and deliverables;

(2) Quality and timeliness of program implementation;

(3) Program performance against approved plans, milestones and budgets;

(4) Quality of monitoring, evaluation, MIS and program reporting;

(5) Effective management and development of program teams;

(6) Effective engagement with program implementation partners and relevant stakeholders;

(7) Identification and mitigation of program-level risks;

(8) Continuous improvement, innovation and learning across the program portfolio;

(9) Evidence of program impact and contribution towards scale and sustainability.

**(4) QUALIFICATIONS, EXPERIENCE AND COMPETENCIES:**

**Qualifications and Experience:**

(1) Postgraduate degree in Social Sciences, Management, Development Studies, MBA or a related discipline from a reputed institution;

(2) Minimum 15 years of relevant professional experience, including significant leadership experience in livelihoods, skilling, employability, entrepreneurship development, workforce development or related sectors;

(3) Demonstrated experience in leading and scaling large, multi-state livelihoods/skilling programs or organizations, with responsibility for strategy, program delivery, people and financial management;

(4) Proven track record of business development and fundraising from CSR, foundations, bilateral and multilateral agencies, philanthropic organizations and other institutional donors;

(5) Demonstrated experience in developing and managing strategic partnerships with government, corporates, industry, development partners and other ecosystem stakeholders;

(6) Experience in managing large and diverse teams across multiple geographies and building high-performing organizations;

(7) Experience in organizational development, institutional strengthening and building systems and processes to support sustainable growth and scale;

(8) Prior experience with P&L/portfolio-level responsibility and strong understanding of financial and operational management would be an advantage.

**Key Skills and Competencies:**

(1) Strong strategic and entrepreneurial leadership experience in livelihoods, skilling, employability and/or entrepreneurship development;

(2) Deep understanding of the livelihoods ecosystem, market trends, employability and market-led livelihood solutions;

(3) Proven ability to develop and execute strategies for program growth, sustainability, innovation and scale;

(4) Strong business development, fundraising and partnership-building skills across CSR, corporates, government, foundations and development partners;

(5) Demonstrated experience in leading large-scale, multi-state programs and managing diverse, high-performing teams;

(6) Strong financial, analytical and decision-making skills, with experience in budgeting and portfolio management;

(7) Excellent communication, stakeholder management and representation skills, with the ability to build national and international networks;

(8) High personal and professional integrity, with a strong commitment to creating sustainable economic opportunities for underserved communities and willingness to travel extensively.

**5. IDEAL CANDIDATE PROFILE:**

The position requires strong experience in leading complex programs in the skilling, employability and/or entrepreneurship development sector, with demonstrated ability to translate strategy into high-quality program delivery, build effective teams and deliver measurable social impact at scale.

**6. COMPENSATION OFFERED:**
Salary shall be commensurate with experience.

**7. LOCATION:**
